---

A note that is not a licence term, because a licence cannot carry it.

This project recognises Kurdish Sign Language. The signs, and the written words they
map to, have to be validated with deaf signers of the dialect they are meant for and
with Kurdish speakers — not taken from a dictionary, and not assumed correct because
the code is. A wrong translation asserted confidently is the harm this project is
built to avoid, and no amount of testing on this side of the camera can rule it out.

Recordings of a person's hands are theirs. If you publish a signs file, publish one
whose signers agreed to it.
